        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "“Rose Cottage”                                  \r\n Crufty, Beamore, Drogheda, Co Louth .   A92E40V \r\n on c 0.667 Acre.\r\n\r\nLOCATION:\r\nEircode is: A92 E40V\r\n\r\nSuits an enterprising person seeking a cottage residence, with great scope to enlarge, or replace, in a much sough after area, where obtaining planning permission for a separate home is so difficult.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\nRose Cottage is a traditional detached stone-built cottage set on a generous site of approximately 0.667 acres, conveniently positioned close to the roadside.\r\nThe cottage extends to approximately 65–70 sq. m. and presents an excellent opportunity for refurbishment, with significant potential for future development, subject to the necessary planning permissions. The cottage building is located on the front right corner of the site leaving the remainder of the site  open for potential uses and development\r\n\r\nThere is a large double garage close to the dwelling, with great scope.\r\nIn addition, there is an agri style barn at the end of the site.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\nThe Cottage is a traditional style cottage, in good order, having been upgraded  a number of years ago. \r\nIt  comprises a small entrance hallway leading into an open-plan living room and kitchen, together with one bedroom and a shower room.\r\nUpstairs, the cottage benefits from a loft area accessed via a spiral staircase, incorporating a small additional sleeping area.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nThe property is set within a large, mature and currently overgrown garden, providing an abundance of outdoor space. To the rear is a double garage and workshop, offering valuable storage and useful additional space with potential for a variety of purposes.\r\nThe cottage occupies the south-western corner of the site, leaving a substantial portion of the grounds available for consideration of future development, subject to planning approval.\r\nGiven the size and configuration of the site, there may be potential for the replacement of the existing dwelling or the construction of an additional house, subject to obtaining the necessary planning permission.\r\n\r\nOpportunity\r\nRose Cottage represents an exciting opportunity for purchasers seeking a character property and renovation project with substantial development potential. The existing cottage could be refurbished to create a cosy permanent residence or attractive holiday home, while the generous site offers longer-term investment possibilities.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.    Folio : MH 25598"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ACCOMMODATION: \r\n  \r\nHallway: Tiled floor, wooden skirting.\r\n\r\nKitchen/living: Tiled and wooden floor. Stove features a red brick surround. \r\nSpiral staircase to loft room.\r\n\r\nLoft room: Velux window, \r\n\r\nBedroom 1: \r\n\r\nShower room: WC, shower, wash hand basin."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "GARDEN & GROUNDS:\r\nTaking a walk on the wild side ..\r\n\r\nThe rear garden is wild and wonderfully overgrown, with a natural, almost botanical garden feel. \r\n\r\nMature trees spill across the space with informal planting gives it an untamed character. It has a feeling of tranquility and escape.\r\n\r\nA private haven from the outside world."
      },
